% Which outcome a group gives does not depend on how far its rows were
% walked.  A sum over rows of which one is not an integer has no value
% even when the integers before it already total past the 64-bit range:
% the type comes before the range, so -vv notes it once and nothing
% fails.  A key with no rows sums to zero, and has no min and no note.
v(a, 9223372036854775807). v(a, 1). v(a, x).
v(b, 9223372036854775807). v(b, x). v(b, 1).
k(a). k(b). k(c).

typed(K, S) :- k(K), S = sum(Z) { v(K, Z) }.
least(K, M) :- k(K), K = c, M = min(Z) { v(K, Z) }.

typed(K, S)?
least(K, M)?
